  "summary_en": "California Assembly Bill 489 (Chapter 615, approved October 2025) extends existing prohibitions on falsely implying health care licensure to developers and deployers of AI and generative AI systems. It bans AI advertising or functionality implying care is provided by a licensed professional, with board enforcement and per-use violations.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Licensure-term prohibitions are enforceable against entities that develop or deploy AI/GenAI using such terms.",
   "Bans AI terms implying advice or care comes from a licensed natural person.",
   "Health care licensing boards have jurisdiction and may seek injunctions.",
   "Each use of a prohibited term is a separate violation.",
   "Adds Chapter 15.5 to the Business and Professions Code."
  ],
